    {
        "content": "<p>fitzgen opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15034\">PR #15034</a> from <code>fitzgen:lazy-lenders</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This commit introduces a <code>lazy_lenders</code> buffer on <code>VMStoreContext</code>. When we need to push a lender for a resource borrow, but haven't forced the lazy thread context yet, we push to <code>lazy_landers</code>. This avoids forcing the lazy thread context, like we previously did. Each <code>VMDeferredThread</code> keeps a watermark of the <code>lazy_lenders</code> length upon construction so that, when we do something that <em>does</em> force the lazy thread context, we can partition <code>lazy_lenders</code> by each thread context that is responsible for those borrows.</p>\n<p>This does <em>not</em> change what is inlined in Wasm code or what is done in libcalls. In the inline exit-sync-call fast path, we bail out to the host when there are lazy lends to be undone. The host libcall still takes care to avoid forcing the <code>VMDeferredThread</code> right before we exit the call in this case.</p>\n<p>Follow up commits will move a bunch of this work inline into the adapters, but I wanted to keep this introduction of <code>lazy_lenders</code> as small as I could.</p>\n<p>Even so, this is a significant speedup for <code>cm-online-stats</code>, our adapter-call-heavy Sightglass benchmark:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">execution</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">instructions</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">retired</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">cm</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">online</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">stats</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">lazy</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">lenders</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">libengine</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">dylib</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">8.4852</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">8.4854</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">faster</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">than</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">main</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">libengine</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">dylib</span><span class=\"o\">!</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">confidence</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">99</span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">0.0001</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"err\">┌────────────┬────────────┬───────────────┬───────────────┬────────┬──────────────────────────────┐</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"err\">│</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Min</span><span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"err\">│</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Max</span><span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"err\">│</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mean</span><span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"err\">│</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Median</span><span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"err\">│</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Noise</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"err\">│</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Engine</span><span class=\"w\">                       </span><span class=\"err\">│</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"err\">├────────────┼────────────┼───────────────┼───────────────┼────────┼──────────────────────────────┤</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"err\">│</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">819957895</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"err\">│</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">827344185</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"err\">│</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">820584935.77</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"err\">│</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">819983269.00</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"err\">│</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">0.014</span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">│</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lazy</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">lenders</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">libengine</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">dylib</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">│</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"err\">├────────────┼────────────┼───────────────┼───────────────┼────────┼──────────────────────────────┤</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"err\">│</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">6957508999</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">│</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">6980867062</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">│</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">6962057536.66</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">│</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">6957759525.50</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">│</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">0.192</span><span clas