        "content": "<p>github-actions[bot] added the label <code>wasmtime:api</code> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15034\">PR #15034</a>.</p>",
        "id": 635540320,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793144671
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> cfallin submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15034#pullrequestreview-5692646662\">PR review</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Thanks! This rates as \"plausible\" to me only because I'm not deeply familiar with the borrow machinery here; @alexcrichton should probably look it over too. Just a few comments I noted below as I read through.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635887957,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793246517
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> cfallin created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15034#discussion_r4408521164\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>\"Watermark\" to me implies some sort of lazy \"max seen so far\" behavior; this is really just \"start of our segment in <code>lazy_lenders</code>\", right? So <code>lazy_lenders_index</code> or <code>lazy_lenders_start</code> might be more clear?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635887983,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793246518
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> cfallin created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15034#discussion_r4408531994\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>We could avoid the smallvec clone here with a hypothetical <code>components_data.lazy_lenders_and_task_state_mut()</code> returning a split borrow, perhaps (similar to the trick we play in a bunch of instances on <code>StoreOpaque</code>)?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635888006,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793246518
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>cfallin requested <a href=\"https://github.com/alexcrichton\">alexcrichton</a> for a review on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15034\">PR #15034</a>.</p>",
        "id": 635888032,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793246527
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>fitzgen updated <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15034\">PR #15034</a>.</p>",
        "id": 636032788,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793286786
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>fitzgen updated <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15034\">PR #15034</a>.</p>",
        "id": 636040038,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793288061
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> alexcrichton submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15034#pullrequestreview-5704575334\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 636122034,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793307401
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15034#discussion_r4417581816\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A few thoughts on this:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>One possibly more-optimizable shape here would be to store the number of lazy lens per-frame rather than storing the current length before the frame in the frame. That way if nothing actually does a borrow then this never even looks at <code>lazy_lenders_start</code>.</li>\n<li>Is <code>band</code> the right way to generate good clif here? I'd expect we'd have better codegen from two <code>icmp</code> + <code>brif</code> instructions as opposed to a <code>band</code> which'd require a bunch of <code>seto</code> and <code>test</code> and such. Perhaps arguably something to happen in ISLE too, but my guess is that our current codegen for <code>brif(band(icmp(...), icmp(...)))</code> is pretty bad</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636122036,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793307402
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15034#discussion_r4417598936\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Subjectively I'd say we could probably get away with a much smaller value here, even something like 4 or maybe 8. This seems relatively difficult to fill in conventional components where there's not all that much cross-component-talk and fast paths generally need just one or two slots.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636122037,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793307402
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15034#discussion_r4417604800\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>We talked about this briefly elsewhere, but personally I'd say just go ahead and remove this and inline the constant <code>LAZY_LENDERS_CAPACITY</code> everywhere since it seems pretty unlikely we'd want to double this at runtime.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636122038,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793307402
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15034#discussion_r4417610996\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Instead of a packed <code>u64</code> would it make sense for this to be just two <code>u32</code> fields, perhaps with the raw index type itself?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636122039,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793307402
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15034#discussion_r4417618719\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Would it make sense to back this up with a <code>debug_assert!</code>?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636122040,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793307402
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15034#discussion_r4417664360\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Instead of a <code>LazyLendersFull</code> error, could this perhaps return <code>Option&lt;..&gt;</code> where <code>None</code> means \"no you can't push the capacity is full\"</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636122042,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793307402
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15034#discussion_r4417680515\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>How come this is all #[cfg]'d to component-model-async? I'd naively expect the optimization here to equally apply with/without component-model-async</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636122043,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793307402
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15034#discussion_r4417715258\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Would it be possible to just delete this code? This seems like it'll all quickly become dead code as this would otherwise happen in cranelift-compiled code otherwise. I think it's reasonable to add the lazy infrastructure here, but I also think it'd be best to avoid adding pieces that won't survive to the final implementation (where possible)</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636122044,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793307402
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15034#discussion_r4417725307\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This method is mostly a duplicate of what's below, in particular the <code>let guest</code> block and assembling all the borrows and such. Could these methods be combined to share more of the implementation?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636122045,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793307402
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15034#discussion_r4417739283\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Any particular reason to split out reserve/push here? OOM-wise I figure it doesn't really matter if we drop a borrow or two while we're trapping due to OOM</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636122046,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793307403
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15034#discussion_r4417804563\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>We talked a bit about this elsewhere, but I wanted to write this down here too. I think it'd be best to ideally remove the need for this method altogether where the lazy lend is a record of \"here's the borrows we haven't yet accounted for in the official tables\" and then undoing that is a simple \"move the stack pointer\" style operation which needs no sort of destructor or such. That would make actually recording a lazy lend that much faster (just put the resource in a table) and would keep everything consistent I believe as well.</p>\n<p>I'm hopeful that something like this would help simplify both this PR as-is and subsequent PRs to add more infrastructure, but I could also be off-the-mark here</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636122048,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793307403
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15034#discussion_r4417797694\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>To keep raw values, maybe flip this and have the host at <code>u32::MAX</code> and other types as-is?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636122051,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793307403
    }
]